# mutgap4_sys_iosfc_base_extended_pixels_v2: A descriptor's base extendedPixelsOnRight and extendedPixelsOnBottom reach the IOSurface as the surface-level kIOSurfacePlaneExtendedPixels keys (a v1 descriptor's are copied into the v2 form): planeless 16x8 BGRA surfaces with 16 extra columns on the right in 512 bytes (bytesPerRow 64) and in 1024 bytes (bytesPerRow 128), then 8 extra rows at the bottom in 512 and in 1024 bytes, then none (v1 base bytes 0x2a and 0x2b; v2 base +0x4c and +0x50), the first of them the process's first map, each mapped then tested; each status and data page is locked. Measured: for a planeless surface IOSurface ignores both keys (unlike the plane-level ones), and every surface maps and the test writes its allocation (so neither the keys nor their copy from v1 shows here).
